## Program Outcome

The hosted App Server fleet screen truthfully reports current readiness and bounded real-execution
performance so operators can assess adoption, reliability, latency, and token overhead by role.

## M1-TRUTHFUL-PERFORMANCE-WORK2 — Correct and size the App Server view

Status: active
Depends on: none

Outcome: Replace selection-derived counters with a privacy-safe aggregate over actual App Server
execution telemetry, retain current readiness and fallback context, extend the hosted contract and
read model, and present compact 24-hour, 7-day, and 30-day performance views (defaulting to 7 days)
on the combined Work2 target.

Gates:

- `G1-REAL-EXECUTION-TRUTH`: actual top-level planning, verification, and CAMP runs drive attempts
  and outcomes; preference, selection, and recovery-control events do not.
- `G2-READINESS-AND-WINDOW-TRUTH`: readiness, observation time, report freshness, explicit 24-hour
  selected bounded window, and browser-local last execution are distinct and correct.
- `G3-PERFORMANCE-SIZING`: the screen shows role breakdown, reliability posture, duration
  percentiles, token intensity, cache ratio, and weighted usage proxy with honest labels.
- `G4-PRIVACY-AND-WORK2`: the strict allowlist, focused tests, combined-target deployment, browser
  checks, release cohort, checkpoint/rebuild proof, and strict Doctor pass.

Candidate campaign: `implement-app-server-dashboard-performance-truth`.

## Work2 Boundary

Work2 includes local aggregate implementation, report schema and hosted persistence changes,
migration, the compact App Server fleet presentation, focused aggregation/privacy/ingest/rendering
tests, quick changed-path validation, a scoped product commit, deployment to the combined live
`ts.rookaro.com` target, authenticated browser and public health checks, release-cohort
registration, Hybrid checkpoint/rebuild proof, and strict Doctor.

Work2 does not push Git, tag or publish a Tool Shed release, add long-term time-series analytics,
claim GUI savings or billing cost, alter App Server routing/qualification, or mark this roadmap and
its owning map terminal. Formal release and outcome reconciliation remain for Work5.

## Deferred Follow-on

After the bounded-window contract is proven, a later PRM may add retained hourly/daily trend
storage and explicitly matched GUI/App Server comparison evidence.
